    text: Removed only the unrelated generated managed-extension timestamp delta after checking all other managed state bytes match the PR base. Item/history mutations and evidence remain canonical PM operations. The preview repair has no extension-manager changes.
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T00:31:54.909Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Shared final-source verification now passes on related canonical owner pm-gh1364: producing receipt test-local-muq885vf-vje4y3 is attributed to source 92cff9ef184f8b6e932afccc999b24c86f070c30 and records 9501 passed cases, zero failures and two platform skips, with all four exact 100-percent coverage dimensions and observed integer totals. The coverage summary hash and fifteen actual measurements are attached to the producing receipt; no focused command is relabeled as corpus evidence. Existing snapshot/semantic receipts and three pre-fix filesystem failures remain independently traceable. Complete final-source static and configured final-head review are pending; live telemetry is unrun."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T04:57:33.162Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final pre-publication review correction: replaced the newly introduced inline filesystem type import with a top-level type namespace import. TypeScript transpileModule confirms byte-identical JavaScript before/after; production source and its coverage denominator are unchanged. Canonical focused receipt test-local-muqhp1g1-rx5nbb passes snapshot and semantic-preview regressions; focused ESLint, all four type configurations and repository docstring gate pass. Canonical tracker receipt test-local-muqhlhtg-bipsvh passes terminal defect contracts, history/resolution validation, all tracker-context assertions and record integrity. Historical receipt restoration independently matches every latest immutable history state. Final-head hosted checks/reviews will rerun after publishing; no pending checks are claimed passed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T06:08:08.827Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Latest review correction isolates root-layout storage and search caches, resolves schema paths from captured pure configuration without source scaffolding, remaps absolute in-root schema paths only in the disposable copy, and rejects external schema paths with transaction_preview_external_schema. Committed journal replays now report validated=false/state=replayed_committed_plan consistently through SDK, CLI, and MCP. Isolated focused proof passes 54 cases and all four exact module coverage dimensions; this is bounded module proof, not repository coverage. Final ownership audit and full-source/static verification remain pending."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T06:17:19.557Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Independent source review identified two additional semantic snapshot inputs: runtime/session.json can supply the focused parent for create, and legal registered item folders may be configured beneath search/runtime/locks. The staging correction now retains the canonical session file and explicit registered storage while excluding unrelated transient siblings. Root-layout context-intent declarations are retained so malformed declarations or concurrent changes cannot disappear from validation. Each correction has real isolated pre-fix failure proof; aggregate source verification will cover the final combined implementation."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T07:08:39.810Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Manual final-source acceptance found an additional actionable CLI dry-run boundary: configuring a missing absolute in-root statuses schema then invoking item mutate --dry-run creates that schema in the source before preview staging. The structured mutate and complete adapters readSettings before preview, and readSettingsWithMetadata calls ensureRuntimeSchemaFileScaffold; configured external schema paths can likewise be touched before containment. The direct SDK snapshot owner is source-preserving, but the CLI promise of dry-run without writing must also cover its startup/preparation reads. Reuse this canonical semantic-preview defect owner. Source is frozen while the current aggregate finishes; the forthcoming correction will use real CLI regressions for missing in-root/external configuration and exact durable-byte preservation, without preinitializing the missing fixture or weakening assertions. Manual failing output is retained and its temporary workspace was cleaned."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T07:50:48.232Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Extended real CLI startup investigation confirms two more owned durable-write paths before/around preview: default preAction runs pending extension migrations, adding extension-migrations.json and workspace history; telemetry startup can scaffold actual global schemas and initialize an absent installation ID. A detached telemetry flush worker cannot inherit the selected-root preparation scope. The correction therefore suppresses owned migration/first-use consent preparation for recognized structured dry-runs, scopes source and exact global configuration reads, retains an existing consented identity for local derived event capture, and avoids creating identities or launching detached flush from the preview. Later normal apply must retain ordinary migration, consent and flushing behavior. Genuine pending-migration pre-fix failures are retained; isolated correction tests are still running. Arbitrary extension activation/preCommand side effects remain an explicit constraint, and local queued events will not be described as collector delivery."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T08:24:15.863Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Isolated correction proof passed 218/218 cases across seven existing regression owners, with fresh build/typecheck/changed-file ESLint. Genuine controls reproduced source/global schema scaffolding, pending extension migrations, and absent identity/settings/history creation before correction; the final SDK transaction module alone has zero coverage deficits (273 statements, 164 branches, 59 functions, 248 lines). This module receipt is not aggregate source coverage. Added linked CLI/settings/fs/telemetry host owners and the canonical focused command. Shared full-source verification remains pending. Independent review is now checking a potential extension-added required option consuming --dry-run as its value: true preview protection must not suppress normal apply hydration or global preparation, so this is under investigation before final source freeze."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T09:59:03.633Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CLI preview startup correction is now settled by the actual Commander action. A conservative literal candidate protects selected/bootstrap/global base-settings reads and parser failures. The first root preAction resolves the real canonical command and effective inherited optsWithGlobals before existing host preparation, enabling or disabling only this invocation-owned AsyncLocalStorage layer. No cloned extension grammar, double activation, global scope mutation, or caller-policy release is used. Real previews skip host-owned schema scaffolding, pending migration execution, first-use consent, installation identity creation and external delivery workers; ordinary apply retains those preparations. Explicit caller scopes and unrelated/concurrent roots remain intact.\n\nThe same seven canonical owners passed 228/228 in the isolated copy. Genuine negative controls cover consumed --dry-run values with ordinary identity/schema/migration preparation, real previews with required package values or namespace flags before the leaf, cross-command package booleans, parser failures and inherited consent. Reverting only the inherited consent guard produces one actual prompt failure; restoring the exact source passes. Existing real filesystem/staged lifecycle controls remain. Focused transaction-module coverage is 273/273 statements,164/164 branches,59/59 functions,248/248 lines; this is not whole-source evidence.\n\nThe unchanged SDK boundary gate caught a private bootstrap-scanner import on canonical receipt test-local-muqs4s2a-ppyog6; all four type configurations passed, but that receipt remains failed. The isolated two-line correction now uses the public global flag contracts, including canonical --pm-path value arity for --path, with no allowlist expansion or new test-only export. The original boundary failure and five tracker-selection failures when only path arity is removed are retained. Exact corrected source passes build, ESLint, boundary and all 228 cases. Shared final static/coverage/package proof is pending on this source.\n\nPre-boundary frozen-source whole-corpus producing receipt test-local-muqsgn28-ortk6u on pm-gh1364 passed 9591 cases, zero failed, two Windows-only skips and exact100 in every dimension (lines63301/63301,statements66369/66369,functions13726/13726,branches50811/50811). Fifteen observed measurements and summary hash80c472e674c90ef42cdb09b8806ed9a5a5729af294f6679afc33f11d5329401c were attached only to that actual passing receipt. This is preserved historical evidence before the import correction, not final-source coverage. Manual temporary acceptance on that artifact passed seven scoped recovery replays, three refusal-parity cases, ordered preview/apply, committed replay, missing absolute in-root schema and external schema refusal, plus complete30 list/30search/26context populations; owned temporary files were removed. Exact final artifact validation remains pending.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T10:01:41.385Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The complete static aggregate reached the baseline contract snapshot check after docstrings, dead exports, ESLint, all three duplicate corpora, workflow permissions, cooldown and generated wrappers passed. It correctly refused the stale fixture: the new transaction_preview_external_schema usage refusal was present in generated source catalogs but absent from the baseline fixture. The package-owned contracts generator refreshed only that one 17-line error-code record; the snapshot check now passes. No contract/gate denominator, scanner allowlist, threshold or manually authored snapshot entry was weakened. This generated fixture is linked to the canonical owner. Complete static aggregate will rerun; the failed receipt remains failed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T10:52:34.145Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Investigation disposition: the proposed extension required-value/tracker-selection defect was falsified by actual CLI controls. Separate --package-note --pm-path/--path is consumed as an ancestor global option by Commander, then refuses the missing package value with usage exit 2 before dispatch; all four original/current controls preserve source and global durable bytes. Attached --package-note=--pm-path/--path validates the real preview with both default and explicitly selected tracker roots; all eight current controls pass and preserve absent schema/identity state. Four fresh built controls at committed 16bb75f47 reproduce the same refusal, and the relevant bootstrap/selection/namespace files match the pre-PR baseline. No tracker-scope expansion or new defect item is warranted by these results."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T12:23:00.599Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Temporary three-step preview preserves source hashes and actual apply reaches closed; committed replay is validated=false with replayed_committed_plan; missing contained absolute schema is staged only, external schema refuses with usage2 and unchanged bytes. Required-value, namespace, parser-error and inherited-consent controls pass; isolated reversion detects real consent and tracker-arity failures. Final corrected source: producing receipt test-local-muqw5il0-81bh9y passes 9591 cases, zero failures, two Windows-only skips and exact100/100/100/100 across760 coverage files (lines63301, statements66369, functions13726, branches50811 all fully covered; summarySHA256 80c472e674c90ef42cdb09b8806ed9a5a5729af294f6679afc33f11d5329401c). All1452 frozen authoring/config/test/doc digests remain unchanged. Focused seven-owner228-case CLI/SDK contracts and temporary manual current-artifact acceptance pass. Canonical type/ESLint/SDK-boundary proof passes; complete static prefix passes source/docs/duplicates/contracts/error catalogs/workflow/agent-context47/gate-registry/public-surface checks. Node24.12 official SDK import admission passes. Matched official CLItransport baseline16bb/current controls both pass all six unchanged latency/RSS budgets with10 measured samples per command; no cause for earlier failed samples is established. Canonical test-local-muqxn5c3-9l1c4s passes graph-composition9 assertions (prose gaps1236 at unchanged ceiling), record-integrity1 assertion and bounded mutation329 killed/336 with seven existing declared equivalents. Failed coverage/performance/static attempts remain failed. Current context/package receipt test-local-muqt3kve-ua5tys passes58 token/context surfaces,89 package-first commands, nine packed npx/bunx packages and artifact19981526<20000000bytes. Registrypositive164/164 members across55 lineages/112edges passes; synthetic unregistered two-member negativecontrol correctly fails. This closes verified implementation for the reviewed PR; exact final-head hosted reviews/checks, merge, main workflows and registry publication remain separate pending stages."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T06:22:17.080Z","harness:codex","Snapshot ownership follows semantic inputs, not directory names: preserve custom registered item folders, captured schemas, context-intent declarations, and the canonical focused-parent session even under transient namespaces. Pure configuration discovery prevents source scaffolding, captured-byte checks catch discovery races, and committed journal replay must disclose that no fresh step validation occurred. CLI/MCP add transport proof while real SDK persistence owns lifecycle semantics."
  "2026-10-02T07:24:44.212Z","harness:codex","A non-writing SDK preview does not guarantee a non-writing CLI dry-run: command registration, extension discovery, author lookup and post-action preparation can call the normal settings hydrator before or after staging. A real CLI boundary must prove that missing configured source/external schemas are neither created nor followed; preinitializing those fixtures hides the defect. Keep startup reads scoped to the selected source root while allowing normal staged hydration and later apply behavior."
  "2026-10-02T09:59:05.127Z","harness:codex","A non-writing preview must cover CLI startup and error cleanup, not only the staged SDK transaction. Protect conservative literal candidates while discovering configuration, then settle only the invocation-owned policy from the actual parser command and effective inherited options before host preparation. Required extension values, namespace flags and parser failures make cloned grammars unsafe. Keep caller scopes composable and prove ordinary apply still performs hydration, identity and migration work. Use published flag contracts rather than widening private-import allowlists; negative controls must isolate the exact arity or consent regression."
